 43,000 pounds of trash from a long-standing dumping site outside Converse in Bexar County. The property had previously been used as an encampment and had drawn years of complaints. The county initially received a $100,000 cleanup estimate before River Aid San Antonio organized volunteer efforts. A final cleanup is planned for November 7.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/around-170-volunteers-remove-43000-pounds-of-trash-from-san-antonio-dumping-site-after-years-of-complaints-property-was-a-homeless-encampment-and-had-a-100000-cleanup-estimate/articleshow/134489475.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/around-170-volunteers-remove-43000-pounds-of-trash-from-san-antonio-dumping-site-after-years-of-complaints-property-was-a-homeless-encampment-and-had-a-100000-cleanup-estimate/articleshow/134489475.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-25T22:11:10+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134489529,imgsize-129786.cms"/></item></channel></rss>